### metamorphic-folds
- Tuinstra, Peterson, Kutlesa, Elgin, Kron and Volkman, "Interconversion between two unrelated protein folds
  in the lymphotactin native state" (*PNAS* 105:5057, 2008): lymphotactin (Ltn, XCL1) is in equilibrium
  between the canonical chemokine fold, Ltn10 — a monomeric three-stranded β-sheet with a C-terminal helix —
  and Ltn40, a dimeric all-β arrangement with no similarity to other known proteins (PDB 2JP1, a homodimer).
  Both are significantly populated in physiological conditions and roughly equally populated near them, and
  the exchange is slow on the NMR chemical-shift timescale, so the spectrum shows both. Tyler, Murray,
  Peterson and Volkman (*Biochemistry* 50:7077, 2011) measured the rates by stopped-flow fluorescence —
  Ltn40 → Ltn10 at 0.4 s⁻¹ and Ltn10 → Ltn40 at 1.4 s⁻¹ at 308 K — in close agreement with 2D exchange NMR
  (0.4 and 1.2 s⁻¹), and found that native-state interconversion requires global unfolding. Conditions set
  the equilibrium: at 200 mM NaCl and 10 °C Ltn10 alone is populated, at 0 mM and 40 °C Ltn40 dominates, and
  replacing Arg23 or Arg43 with alanine raises the Ltn10 population even without salt. Ltn10 is the form that
  activates the receptor XCR1.
- *Claude's gloss:* the clearest instance of the claim in its exact form. One sequence fixes two basins,
  their rates and the dependence of both on salt, temperature and named residues, all reproducible and
  measured; the exception is to "one sequence, one structure", which is a claim about a point, and not to the
  determinacy of the fiber. The carrier is `Taut` with the basins as points: `Taut A step` takes any type of
  forms and any transition relation, and nothing in it is specific to protons. `taut-respects` then says a
  property differing between Ltn10 and Ltn40 — receptor activation — cannot be stated of the two-fold
  carrier at all, only of a basin, which is to say of an observation that picks one out. The NMR result is
  `ic-within` run by an instrument: the chemical-shift timescale is a window, exchange at about 1 s⁻¹ is
  slower than it, so NMR reports two forms, while an assay averaging over minutes reports one equilibrium —
  the shape `td-one-in-a-day` and `td-two-in-ten-minutes` prove for thalidomide, and the shape ring
  conformational averaging takes in `nmr-orbits`. Ltn40 is also `orbit-invariant`'s case: the automorphism
  exchanging the two chains of the homodimer puts corresponding residues in one orbit, which is why a
  symmetric dimer gives one set of resonances. Two encodings of the window are now written, and they meet
  here. `Interconv` holds half-lives in whole minutes, so lymphotactin's (about 1.7 s and 0.5 s) round to
  zero, which `ic-within` reads as no interconversion — `kek-one-substance` already sits at "the shortest
  window the carrier can state". The setting layer (`Motion`, `Setting`, `motion-admitted`,
  `signals-under`) holds rates as orders of magnitude in inverse seconds and the observation's resolving
  rate beside them, which is lymphotactin's scale: exchange at about 10⁰ s⁻¹ against a proton resolving
  rate of 10² to 10³ s⁻¹ is not admitted, so the spectrum shows two forms, as cyclohexane's chair flip is
  not admitted below its coalescence temperature. A `Motion` is a permutation of atoms, and a fold switch
  permutes none — Ltn10 and Ltn40 have one bond graph — so the switch is a transition between forms, in
  `Taut`, timed by the setting's test.
