- What 100% accuracy is, stated in (1.1)–(1.3). The experiment is itself a reading: a crystal structure is a
  `Report` whose value is coordinates and whose warrant is the diffraction data and the refinement, and its
  fiber is every structure that warrant admits. NMR deposits the family literally — PDB 2JP1, lymphotactin's
  alternative fold, records 100 conformers calculated and 20 submitted. So agreement with experiment is
  defined up to the experiment's own warrant, and 100% accuracy is two properties together: *soundness*, the
  observed reading lies in the predicted family for every target, and *tightness*, the predicted family is no
  wider than the experiment's.
- `vacuous-report`, `Informative` and `unit-warrant-not-informative` already separate them: a predictor that
  outputs every conformation of the chain is sound on every target and refuses nothing. Soundness alone is
  free; "solved" is soundness with tightness. Soundness holds by construction (`protein-carrier`); tightness
  is where information enters, and there are four sources of it — transport from the fold class
  (`fold-space-transport`), coevolution (`coevolution-couplings`), the handedness the chain forces
  (`fold-handedness`), and the physics (`folding-determinism`).
- The field's own record of where it stands. The CASP16 monomer assessment (*Proteins*, 2025,
  doi:10.1002/prot.70031) reports single-domain fold prediction nearly solved, with no target fold predicted
  incorrectly across all groups; the round's overview says AlphaFold2 at CASP14 largely solved monomers, often
  at accuracy comparable to experiment. The complex assessment (doi:10.1002/prot.70068) reports complex
  prediction unsolved, with the leading groups predicting slightly more than half the targets to high
  accuracy.
- *Claude's gloss:* the open region is complexes, proteins with more than one state, and ligands with their
  stereochemistry — exactly where a carrier whose output is one point fails. A complex adds the assembly's
  symmetry and stoichiometry, which is `Orbit`; a multi-state protein is a fiber with more than one basin,
  which is `Taut`; a ligand brings `Cyc`. The remaining error sits where the representation lacks the object.
